text \<open>
  The intended comparison preserves the decisions on the supplied argument
  domain. Each observation therefore retains its Boolean outcome, including
  refusal. Inclusion of these complete graphs is exactly agreement. Increasing
  the positive set alone can lose an original refusal.

  Both witnesses are formed programs with actual entries. Equal empty positive
  meanings can hide different call boundaries. Equal complete call boundaries
  can hide opposite truth. Each failure supplies the omitted facet and its
  concrete outcome through the existing candidate-loss account. The two-facet
  basis is therefore irredundant for this whole comparison scope.

  The same exact reduction evaluates these comparisons. Physical code retention,
  native availability, and establishment obligations remain different questions;
  decision agreement does not identify their programs or prove those properties.

  The finite execution computes the actual interface and positive-meaning
  observations of these three programs at two supplied arguments. Proved code
  equations replace only this calculation. The complete table, intended
  comparison, and residual equations retain their independent contracts.
  Both Boolean outcomes are encoded, so a missing positive call remains
  observable. Numeric coordinates are private to this finite investigation;
  its sample scope does not replace the general comparison proved above.
\<close>

